I decided to clear the altar by zapping a /oTele at it. Later, this level
would spawn Archons, and it looked like someone fired a gigantic shotgun at
it. What a wonderful idea! Monsters zapping wands of digging added a "nice"
flavour to this level.



After getting a new BoH (well, actually two) and stuff to fill them, I set out
to level 1. I'd keep a BoH named "ShoppingBag" with me, and only kept my 
"End Run" BoH either in a box or Ludios.
I wanted to eliminate the possibility of putting something stupid inside my
BoH after doing so once in this game.

On turn 21000 +, I had already both gotten 20 extra protection points and
done some mass-torching on various levels. I was already on experience level
30, so I decided to travel to level 1 and kill all remaining monsters in
a more strict order.


217529. Level 1-4 clear. Liches are toughest monsters that come.
218295. Level 5 (Oracle) Baby monsters! Urgh!
224420. Level 5: End of baby monsters.
224961. Level 6: glass golems, demiliches
225155. Level 8: giants, angels
225377. Level 10: dragons
226759. Level 12: rest of ki-rins
227387. Level 14: mastodon(s)
228113. Level 22: Archons, but doesn't last for long. Small panic grips me
as I realize that Archons are created spontaneously, too! Charmed total 5
Archons, they killed the rest. It took me some time to realize and apply
this tactic to battle them. 

229000+: Level 30, VoD. With 3 Archons, we battle the Hell's minions.
233285: VoD. All archons are dead, including the 2 I left behind.
236594: VoD. Now only arch-liches, fire vortices, salamanders,
sandestins and balrogs...
236945: Hunting for last monsters from all levels. I leave the peaceful
priest of Anhur and Izchak in Minetown.
243181: Getting the final gear, after which I mostly encounter trolls
and monsters inside the Wizard's Tower.

As I got around grabbing my gems, I found out that it was heavy. I had to
leave some 120 gems behind, wear GoP and still be burdened.
Nothing interesting happened during the Amulet Run before the Astral Plane.
There I fought the enemies by Stormy, mostly, or wand/spell of death ray.
Only Pestilence gave me some creeps, but I shot him mostly from afar.
I also left my BoH near the altar of Anhur to venture westwards to face
Pestilence. I got some emergency items, of course, in my oilskin sack.
Then I returned and offered the Amulet of Yendor to Anhur.


Final thoughts / notes:

I'll say again that arch-liches are fun to play. They can't carry much stuff
and the cold melee damage shatters potions, but it hardly matters in an 
extinctionist game. I had to leave tons of potions behind. 
I had lots of stuff in Ludios waiting to be polyed, but there was no point.

The first monster saccings I did one by one, slowly getting my AC from
minus sixtysomething to -93 (wearing gauntlets of dexterity at the time).
Since I figured out that maybe I'd accidentally #pray instead of #offer,
I stopped praying unless I wanted more holy water. 
It was then when I created rooms like:

