I created looots of monsters, and then used the fireball as mentioned earlier.
If the first summoned monster was something horrible, I either teleported away
or killed it quickly.

Even though my xlevel was 30, I quaffed potions of gain level whenever I could.
This way I got lots of energy (wizards get much, of course) and some hp.

On dlevel 4 (Oracle) I got a feeling of despair or disbelief :
"Do I really have to kill 120 of every baby monster? Urgh..." It was
efficient but tedious slaughter. I drained all my mana to summon the
monsters, then hacked at them with Stormy (rinse and repeat). 

In Valley of the Dead, I had lots of "fun" battling with a maximum of 3 Archons
against monsters; I blinded myself (to avoid reading --more--, --more--, and
--more--), read all scrolls of create monster, broke all wands of create monster
and mostly let the Archons do their job. Even if the level was 1/5 full of
monsters, the Archons sliced and diced them (until they died from a mobs summoned
by arch-liches later).

It's a horrible and wonderful experience - a NetHack game to end all NetHack
games for the individual. Then again, maybe not.



